From 682e66e2a64c3ebe74da5ecd0e4d9dda24fa8876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 14:18:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Overhaul auth: single top-level login + section/sub-section
 permissions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New portal_auth.py: shared users/permissions DB used by both the portal
  shell and the mounted Training Tracker app (same session cookie via a
  shared Flask secret key, so logging in once authenticates both).
- Portal app.py: /login, /logout, before_request login gate on every route,
  a route->section map so each Invoice Generator client's API is blocked
  without the matching permission, and a new /admin/permissions screen
  (superadmin-only) to create users and grant section/sub-section access,
  plus Training Tracker's admin/editor/viewer role.
- templates/index.html + static/js/app.js: sidebar nav (top-level tabs and
  Invoice Generator's per-client sub-nav) now only renders what the logged
  -in user has access to; added logged-in-as/logout + Users & Permissions
  link; added an empty state for a user with no access at all.
- Training Tracker: removed its own login/users table entirely (delegates
  to portal_auth for both authentication and its admin/editor/viewer role);
  removed local /admin/users/* routes and admin.html's Users section in
  favor of the portal-level screen; removed the online sign-off feature
  (signoff_sheet/submit_signature routes, sign.html, the 'Open sign-off'
  button) per request — the manager's physical-sheet upload/download flow
  is unchanged. Added a migration for existing installs to safely drop the
  old local users table and the FK on signoff_uploads.uploaded_by.
